		{
			"to": "western-civ/augustus",
			"why": "Augustus took charge of Rome's grain supply in 22 BC and fixed the dole at about 200,000 citizens; Tacitus said he won over the populace \"with cheap corn\"."
		},
		{
			"to": "western-civ/cicero",
			"why": "Clodius, who drove Cicero into exile in 58 BC, made Rome's grain dole free in the same tribunate."
		},
		{
